  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Florida received $22.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 30.0% year over year while award activity reached 153,922 awards with an average award size of $148K. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in Florida, obligating $15.4B, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $2.5B and the General Services Administration with $1.5B. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations at $4.5B, and Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction follows with $2.3B. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION leads vendors with $2.6B and $2.2B entries among the top vendors, and THALLE CONSTRUCTION CO INC obligated $1.9B. Historical context shows obligations peaked in FY25 at $32.5B and then moved to $22.7B in FY26. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in Florida federal contracting year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 30.0% year over year. Total obligations in FY26 are $22.7B compared with $32.5B in FY25. Award count stands at 153,922 with an average award size of $148K. The Department of Defense remains the single largest buyer with $15.4B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who dominates buying and which industries get the most dollars?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $15.4B in FY2026 to date and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $2.5B. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing received $4.5B and Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction received $2.3B. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION, THALLE CONSTRUCTION CO INC, and LOYAL SOURCE GOVERNMENT SERVICES LLC are among the top vendors by obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
