    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Florida?",
      "a": "Florida received $22.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Total award count in the state is 153,922 and the average award size is $148K. Obligations fell 30.0% year over year, down from $32.5B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Florida?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense and the Department of Veterans Affairs are the largest buyers in Florida. The Department of Defense obligated $15.4B, the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $2.5B, and the General Services Administration obligated $1.5B in FY2026 to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest federal contractors in Florida?",
